ASD-STE100 (Simplified Technical English)
-----------------------------------------

The rules in the "base" category (slop-cop's base layer) are original
works, written for this project and released under the MIT License.
They are inspired by ASD-STE100, Simplified Technical English, Issue 9,
15 January 2025, a standard published by ASD (AeroSpace and Defence
Industries Association of Europe), Brussels. ASD holds the copyright in the
standard, and "ASD-STE100" is ASD's trademark, used here nominatively to
identify the standard.

No text of ASD-STE100 is reproduced anywhere in this repository: not its
rule wording, not its examples, and no part of its Dictionary.

The following mapping is bibliographic citation only, recording which parts
of the standard inspired each base rule:

    long-sentence       inspired by STE rule 6.3, at a 40-word threshold
                        rather than the standard's 20/25
    long-paragraph      inspired by STE rule 6.6
    passive-voice       inspired by STE rule 3.6
    agentless-passive   inspired by STE rule 3.6
    padded-verb         inspired by STE rule 3.4
    missing-hyphen      inspired by STE rule 8.2
    term-consistency    inspired by STE rule 1.11, implemented as
                        within-document consistency only, not the standard's
                        approved-noun requirement
    expletive-opener    from general plain-language guidance, not STE
    nominalization      from general plain-language guidance, not STE

Passing slop-cop's checks is NOT conformance with ASD-STE100. The thresholds
deliberately differ from the standard's, the Dictionary-driven rules are not
implemented at all, and slop-cop is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
certified by ASD.

The plain-word substitution list in internal/detectors/plainwords_data.go
was compiled from general English usage references and public-domain
plain-language guidance. It was not derived from the STE Dictionary or from
any reconstruction of it. Two third-party word lists were considered as
sources and rejected: openste/openste and dfch/biz.dfch.AsdSte100Vocab are
unverified reconstructions of ASD-copyrighted content, and the latter both
self-declares that it is not affiliated with or endorsed by ASD and is
licensed AGPL-3.0, which is incompatible with this project's MIT
distribution.

The standard itself is available free of charge from ASD on request at
https://asd-ste100.org, under ASD's own terms, which do not permit general
public redistribution.

